### Odds Format Options
The lucky 31 calculator supports three odds formats. Fractional odds (5/1, 7/2) remain the traditional UK format for horse racing. Decimal odds (6.00, 4.50) show the total return including stake and are popular across European betting markets. American odds (+500, -200) use positive and negative numbers to indicate underdogs and favorites. GB users primarily work with fractional odds, though decimal odds have gained ground since online betting expanded. The calculator converts between formats automatically, ensuring accurate return calculations regardless of input format. Users select their preferred format before entering selection odds for consistent processing across all 31 bets.
## Understanding Your Lucky 31 Bet Breakdown
A Lucky 31 calculator processes returns across 31 separate bets derived from 5 selections. With a £1 unit stake, the total stake reaches £31 because each combination—singles, doubles, trebles, four-fold accumulators, and one five-fold accumulator—counts as an individual wager. Returns accumulate only from winning selections, meaning even a single correct pick triggers payouts across 5 singles bets, while two winners activate 10 doubles and additional singles.
The structure ensures partial returns when not all selections win. If three selections prove correct, bettors receive payouts from 10 singles, 10 doubles, and 10 trebles. Four winners add 5 four-fold accumulators to the tally. Only when all five selections succeed does the five-fold accumulator contribute to the total return.
