The Lucky 31 calculator automatically applies odds to each active bet combination. Higher-priced selections amplify returns exponentially through accumulators, while shorter-priced picks provide steadier, smaller contributions across singles and doubles. Stake management remains critical—total outlay scales with unit stake selection, and losses occur when selections fail to win.
Returns depend entirely on the odds of winning selections and how many succeed. The calculator displays projected returns based on entered odds, allowing bettors to assess potential outcomes before committing funds. All betting carries financial risk, and returns are never guaranteed regardless of calculation accuracy.
## Each Way Lucky 31 Bets Explained
An each way Lucky 31 doubles the bet count to 62 because every combination runs twice—once for the win and once for the place. With a £1 unit stake, total outlay becomes £62. Place terms typically apply at one-quarter or one-fifth of the win odds, depending on the event. The Lucky 31 calculator handles these adjustments automatically when the each way option is selected.
Horse racing represents the primary context for each way betting. Races with five or more runners usually offer place terms, paying out if selections finish within the top positions. The exact number of places paid and the odds fraction vary by race type and field size. National Hunt races often provide more generous place terms than flat racing.
Each way becomes advantageous when backing selections at longer odds in competitive fields. If a selection places but does not win, the place portion still generates returns across the 31 place bets. This structure provides insurance against near misses while maintaining full win potential.
The calculator requires odds entry for each of the 5 selections plus confirmation of place terms. It then computes separate win and place returns, displaying total potential payouts. Bettors should verify place terms with their bookmaker before wagering, as terms differ between operators and events.
Each way Lucky 31 bets demand higher stakes but offer broader coverage. This approach suits horse racing accumulators where consistent placing proves more achievable than outright wins. All gambling involves risk, and losses can double when both win and place bets fail.
